      "apiDescription": "## Props\n\n```\nexport type GToastProps = {\n  /**\n   * @description custom class name for Toast\n   * @default ''\n   */\n  customClass?: string;\n  /**\n   * @description duration before close. It will not automatically close if set 0\n   * @default 5000\n   */\n  duration?: number;\n  /**\n   * @description notification dom id\n   * @default ''\n   */\n  id?: string;\n  /**\n   * @description description text\n   * @default ''\n   */\n  message?: string | VNode<RendererNode, RendererElement, { [key: string]: any; }> | (() => VNode<RendererNode, RendererElement, { [key: string]: any; }>);\n  /**\n   * @description offset from the top edge of the screen. Every Toast instance of the same moment should have the same offset\n   * @default 0\n   */\n  offset?: number;\n  /**\n   * @description callback function when toast clicked\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  onClick?: (() => void);\n  /**\n   * @description custom position\n   * @default 'top-right'\n   */\n  position?: string;\n  /**\n   * @description whether to show a close button\n   * @default true\n   */\n  showClose?: boolean;\n  /**\n   * @description whether to show progress bar\n   * @default true\n   */\n  showProgress?: boolean;\n  /** @description toast size variant */\n  size?: string;\n  /** @description whether `message` is treated as HTML string */\n  dangerouslyUseHTMLString?: boolean;\n  /** @description callback function when closed */\n  onClose: () => void;\n  /** @description toast type - required and determines the icon */\n  type: string;\n  /** @description initial zIndex */\n  zIndex?: number;\n}\n```\n\n## Events\n\n```\nexport type GToastEvents = {\n  destroy: [];\n}\n```\n\n## Slots\n\nEach slot is typed with the props it passes to its content.\n\n```\nexport type GToastSlots = {\n  default: {};\n}\n```\n\n## Exposed\n\nAvailable on the component instance through a template ref.\n\n```\nexport type GToastExposed = {\n  visible: boolean;\n  /** @description close notification */\n  close: () => void;\n}\n```",
